{"title":"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Algebra_+_Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Algebra + Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Basic_calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Basic calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Steve says to Jon, \"I am thinking of a polynomial whose roots are all positive integers. The polynomial has the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59031a6a177df72aa960c576396d1f2f9ef75f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = 2x^3-2ax^2+(a^2-81)x-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"19\" /> for some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Can you tell me the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\"\n</p><p>After some calculations, Jon says, \"There is more than one such polynomial.\"\n</p><p>Steve says, \"You're right.  Here is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\" He writes down a positive integer and asks, \"Can you tell me the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\"\n</p><p>Jon says, \"There are still two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\"\n</p><p>Find the sum of the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Algebra)\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We call the three roots (some may be equal to one another) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.  Using Vieta's formulas, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0cabe349ee2d4c24e0ca371f226077fc3f11406f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+x_3 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6b1399e56dc088e97390cb16be37d8e90bef73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2+x_1 \\cdot x_3+x_2 \\cdot x_3 = \\frac{a^2-81}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"274\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb87b25febd535e6a6803a4bb2c10dad797ed9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = \\frac{c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"33\" />. \n</p><p>Squaring our first equation we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124af5e7280de741f793de7b33ea0b52fc715396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2+x_2^2+x_3^2+2 \\cdot x_1 \\cdot x_2+2 \\cdot x_1 \\cdot x_3+2 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"417\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>We can then subtract twice our second equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddcfdad61811f07026a08b1c36bf3821a25d1d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2+x_2^2+x_3^2 = a^2-2 \\cdot \\frac{a^2-81}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"243\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying the right side:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa8b93a198513a3a36b4679824cc21c4d97bf80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2-2 \\cdot \\frac{a^2-81}{2} &amp;= a^2-a^2+81\\\\ &amp;= 81.\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"242\" height=\"60\" />\n</p><p>So, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7a5151fe169d6fe8b32e03148b32773c1246e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2+x_2^2+x_3^2 = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We can then list out all the triples of positive integers whose squares sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p>We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c99e4dc18c935fba82727826f257ebfcf64989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4, 8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb2967ff90073f255b055fb4db6b6038ea99ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f3c543b71b0cf5b0346e0db8de170a6e89a9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>These triples give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73fc3e1b03ec11ac4a6ecf5313d1a6f433da109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/00000117d679c285532c25fd0d5129a728ca4653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, respectively.  \n</p><p>We know that Jon still found two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> when Steve told him the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> value, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> value must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73fc3e1b03ec11ac4a6ecf5313d1a6f433da109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/00000117d679c285532c25fd0d5129a728ca4653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc7a2b0dc9bac8cebc3978e0f00609c4c816b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{440}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>~BealsConjecture~\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Algebra_.2B_Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Algebra_+_Brute_Force)\">Solution 2 (Algebra + Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Algebra + Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First things first. Vietas gives us the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c666f0d24497db353a11ecec580150bca298fe88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} x_1+x_2+x_3 = a\\\\ x_1 \\cdot x_2+x_1 \\cdot x_3+x_2 \\cdot x_3 = \\frac{a^2-81}{2}\\\\ x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = \\frac{c}{2} \\end{align}\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" />\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must have odd parity, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb171603dfda465e4e115ca674113f2452a81a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which implies that both sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> are even. Then, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we see that an odd number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> must be odd, because we have already deduced that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. In order for both sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> to be even, there must only be one odd number and two even numbers.\n</p><p>Now, the theoretical maximum value of the left side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61361723d7984023c52d94243791c093040b961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\biggl(\\frac{a}{3}\\biggr)^2=\\frac{a^2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"117\" height=\"49\" />. That means that the maximum bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is where\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a49ea17959aadff0fad223447730df8e1aad03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2}{3} &gt; \\frac{a^2-81}{2},\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"39\" />\nwhich simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da34ea6ee547e3dde84465e2a90f8ce88f3c4a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{243} &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" />, meaning\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb2746c782ab3adb3f364431c3a70459e3ab3a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 &gt; a.\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />\nSo now we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7b76abd9c0c9104727746deb764d21568c16ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ceeb62c98e832c5e96b04133c3c8acb0116bd4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is odd from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> could equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. At this point, we have simplified the problem to the point where we can casework+ brute force. As said above, we arrive at our solutions of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c99e4dc18c935fba82727826f257ebfcf64989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4, 8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb2967ff90073f255b055fb4db6b6038ea99ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f3c543b71b0cf5b0346e0db8de170a6e89a9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, of which the last two return equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> values. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2cc6be70b0dc5fb35807b4a8d41fd9f80978e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(3 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 6+4 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 7)=\\boxed{440}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"23\" /> AWD.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Basic_calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Basic_calculus)\">Solution 3 (Basic calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Basic calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each of the roots is positive, the local maximum of the function must occur at a positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e547a65c7d4fe064e52a07834af65b7c310237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{dx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" /> of the polynomial yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e0059b7746dc6d36959e31a643a26b5f71e9e02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x^2-4ax+a^2-81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at the local maximum. Since this is a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we can find an expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The quadratic formula gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d24ba1446575ce75162baff7c95b90c54884d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{4x\\pm\\sqrt{324-8x^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832d503393f9322f4db4f4880c5622a7abdd62d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2x\\pm\\sqrt{81-2x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"160\" height=\"21\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, and testing small positive integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4586b4be64967351da3dabde1e8d89959298f9b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4586b4be64967351da3dabde1e8d89959298f9b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792fa2135a12f746ee8d35f224cc514437dd03c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=9$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd92d02476c3434bf645bf5a3bc249eca83d3c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Because the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> alone does not determine the polynomial, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now our polynomial equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4827345a8fd3b1d4bd75d4432bead9f0be5646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^3-30x^2+144x-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />. Because one root is less than (or equal to) the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value at the local maximum (picture the graph of a cubic equation), it suffices to synthetically divide by small integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to see if the resulting quadratic also has positive integer roots. Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> leaves a quotient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f77c853146f7581d4d4e5a1aea660c915cfa977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2-24x+72=2(x-6)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"21\" />, and dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> leaves a quotient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b928ca517d5110a6e73c1ff4638a95b64d5a7fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2-22x+56=2(x-4)(x-7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d623a3caf71fc8c85aa1ce9ddaf0001dec4bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2\\cdot 3\\cdot 6\\cdot 6=216$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec082bca1924065b41f47e1e20df558fa8cfd01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2\\cdot 4\\cdot 4\\cdot 7=224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c4c563b7e1021669c30fb7bbfd087345d5e4b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216+224=\\boxed{440}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" /> ~bad_at_mathcounts\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re2qLzOKWk&amp;t=427s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re2qLzOKWk&amp;t=427s</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II\" title=\"2015 AIME II\">2015 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235328\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.073 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 594/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18372/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.468      1 -total\n 57.00%    7.107      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.59%    5.060      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14139:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235328 and revision id 189615. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}